\pard\plain \sl288\slmult1\ltrch\loch \f1\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 A painter, a sculptor, these are artists, yes, that\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8217\'92s reasonable to say, but what about a tax collector? Is he an artist too if he plumbs the depths of greed? Is a sheep-shearer plying her shears an artist if she\u8217\'92s sufficiently clever about it? What about a farmer? Give a young man a shovel, a field of dirt, friends to impress, and what does he do? The priest leaves the derivation of the answer as an exercise to the audience. For the prude, the answer is a penis. The average Jandri boy will find it funny to dig a big old ugly in the dirt. He laughs because it doubles as a drainage ditch, just like the real thing. To place such degeneracy in the same category as the cloud of colored windows which open up the ceiling of the Gambagall\hich\f1 \emdash \loch\f1 well! That is an affront to the sacred.}
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 Two days ago, Vigram heard a variation of this sermon. He didn\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8217\'92t normally go into the temple, because that meant he\u8217\'92d have to listen to someone else speak, but he\u8217\'92d gone, and so young Mandrameen was forced to deal with the consequences.}
\par\pard\plain \ltrch\loch \f1\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain \f1\fs24\b0\i0
\par\pard\plain \sl288\slmult1\ltrch\loch {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 Burly, broad-faced Vigram. He, a gleaming scalp with a belly beard. He smacked his rich breakfast table with a fat hand. \loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8220\'93That\u8217\'92s wrong!\u8221\'94 he roared. \u8220\'93If everyone is an artist, then the word is as useful as an unmarked weight!\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain \f1\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram, meanwhile, was tall, and huge. Mandri, operating on the principle that there has never been such a thing as an obese philosopher, doubted everything Vigram said.}
\par\pard\plain \sa180\sb180\ltrch\loch \f1\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 \hich\f1 \emdash \loch\f1 Mandri making clear artist is selfishness here??? I feel like there was a note I am forgetting.}
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 *As Such*\line }
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 We don\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8217\'92t mention Mandri\u8217\'92s farm until the end.}
\par\plain \f1\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain \f1\fs24\b0\i0
\par\pard\plain \sl288\slmult1\ltrch\loch {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 Lora tsked her tongue to check his creeping aggression}
\par\pard\plain \sa180\sb180\ltrch\loch \f1\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 \hich\f1 \emdash \loch\f1 Lora loves to act.}
\par\plain \f1\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 'The majority of my poems go through a vigorous series of revisions. In this instance, I resisted that impulse, as I didn\loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8217\'92t want to fall into the trap of revising the poem to try and keep pace with the escalating and profoundly disturbing violence.'}
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 Gonna be honest, it might have been worth falling into the trap of revising the poem}
